   "date": "2019-08-20T01:16:16Z",
   "subject": "Help with estimate.missing function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Dear\r\nAll,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">I\r\nhave a 3D dataset in morphologika format (17x3x3) with missing values and I´m\r\ntrying to use the function <span>estimate.missing\r\nin Geomorph. I followed the instructions and replaced the -999 with NA values\r\nhowever when I tried to obtain the corresponding missing landmarks estimated I obtained\r\nthis error: <span style=\"color:red\">Error in A[, , j] : subscript out of bounds</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Somebody knows what is happen?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Here I attach my dataset in morphologika format <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Here´s my code:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">mydata&lt;-read.morphologika(&quot;mydata.txt&quot;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">any(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484805401000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2V-iihNE_6dpkC3qDNIVpC\">is.na</a>(mydata))</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">mydata[which(mydata\r\n== -999)] &lt;- NA</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">x&lt;-estimate.missing(mydata,method=&quot;TPS&quot;)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Thanks in advance</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Pablo<br></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "MyIyaDB8AgAJ",
   "from": "Abel Bosman",
   "author": "9bb04f8bd082335c",
   "date": "2019-08-20T09:52:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Help with estimate.missing function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Pablo,</div><div><br></div><div>I took a look at your data and the problem is obvious without even running the code.</div><div>All your specimens have landmark 15 missing.</div><div>The TPS method needs to have a reference specimen for which all landmarks are present. Withouth a complete specimen, neither the TPS nor the Regression method will work.</div><div>Please take a look at the &quot;Details&quot; section in the help section of the &quot;estimate.missing&quot; function. This text states:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\">The first approach (method=&quot;TPS&quot;) uses the thin-plate spline to interpolate landmarks on a reference specimen to estimate the locations of missing landmarks on a target specimen. Here, a reference specimen is obtained from the set of specimens for which all landmarks are present, Next, each incomplete specimen is aligned to the reference using the set of landmarks common to both. Finally, the thin-plate spline is used to estimate the locations of the missing landmarks in the target specimen.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\">So, without a complete specimen, no landmarks can be estimated!!</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\">If the landmark is bilateral (i.e. is present on the other side) and your specimen has object symmetry, you could use reflected relabeling to estimate the missing landmarks. Note that this only works for bilateral homologues, so not if it is a unilateral landmark. Also note that this will make the esimated landmark symmetrical, while your specimens might have an inherent asymmetry (i.e. fluctuating or direction-based). Please consider your research question carefully, as symmetrizing a single landmark while maintaining assymetry in the rest of your sample could bias your results.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\">Best regards,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\">Abel<br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;float:none\"><br></span></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Op di 20 aug. 2019 om 03:16 schreef Pablo Fisichella &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fisiche...@gmail.com</a>&gt;:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Dear\r\nAll,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">I\r\nhave a 3D dataset in morphologika format (17x3x3) with missing values and I´m\r\ntrying to use the function <span>estimate.missing\r\nin Geomorph. I followed the instructions and replaced the -999 with NA values\r\nhowever when I tried to obtain the corresponding missing landmarks estimated I obtained\r\nthis error: <span style=\"color:red\">Error in A[, , j] : subscript out of bounds</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Somebody knows what is happen?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Here I attach my dataset in morphologika format <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Here´s my code:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">mydata&lt;-read.morphologika(&quot;mydata.txt&quot;)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">any(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484805403000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3FQsZ7EcGRtA-R2QX9xV09\">is.na</a>(mydata))</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">mydata[which(mydata\r\n== -999)] &lt;- NA</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">x&lt;-estimate.missing(mydata,method=&quot;TPS&quot;)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Thanks in advance</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Pablo<br></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/c6ab61f9-57df-4a1a-a282-2fffc0017a69%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/c6ab61f9-57df-4a1a-a282-2fffc0017a69%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484805403000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NQzJhxuP7W-u2tbLaKfQm\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/c6ab61f9-57df-4a1a-a282-2fffc0017a69%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
