    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Pablo,</div><div><br></div><div>While this is the geomorph mailing list, I would like to point you towards the Morpho Package.</div><div>This package has a function called &quot;fixLMmirror&quot;, which you should be able to directly apply to your array and performs the reflected relabeling. You just have to supply an extra matrix that contains the rownumbers of the paired bilateral landmarks.</div><div><br></div><div>Best regards,</div><div>Abel<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Op wo 21 aug. 2019 om 13:27 schreef Pablo Fisichella &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fisiche...@gmail.com</a>&gt;:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Abel,</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much for your detailed response. I understand quite well your points. Actually, my missing points are bilateral, I mean I have the left point but not the right one. I´ll try to understand how I can reflect such points.  I´m wondering to know how I can proceed to perform the reflected relabeling you have mentioned.</div><div><br></div><div>All best,</div><div><br></div><div>Pablo<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El lun., 19 ago. 2019 a las 22:16, Pablo Fisichella (&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fisiche...@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Dear\r\nAll,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\